From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:21:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): list a session's links beside its open items

A long session keeps referring to the same few pages (a published report,
a tracker), and the only way back to one is to scroll for the message that
linked it.

The session header's open-items panel gains a Links section, read from the
loaded transcript like the items, with nothing stored:

- Pages are collected without the agent doing anything. A small list of
  matchers (SESSION_LINK_MATCHERS) says which links count; the first one
  takes claude.ai/artifact/<id> and claude.ai/code/artifact/<id> links in
  agent messages. A page is listed once, newest mention first, titled by
  the newest link text written for it. Links in fenced code are skipped.
- A link label pins any other link on purpose: [L1] followed by a bold
  title and the link. It is an ordinary item label, so it numbers,
  previews and closes the same way: ~~[L1]~~ takes the link off the list,
  and with it the collected row for the same page. Link labels are left
  out of the open-items list and its count.

Each link opens the way a link in chat does. The button now also shows
for a transcript that has links but no items.

The item-label instruction every agent gets says how to pin a link. A page
or pin mentioned only in history that has not been loaded is missing until
the reader scrolls up to it, as for items.

Local only: this extends the chat-item-labels series, which is not
upstream, and is not proposed upstream yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
